  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I would like to suggest adding a photosensitivity or epilepsy warning option to VRChat’s existing content tag system.\n\nI’m one of the owners of Latin Gang, one of the largest VRChat animation communities, and many of our creators produce visually intensive content using flashing lights, strobes, rapid color changes, particles, and other effects that may affect photosensitive users.\n\nVRChat already has content tags intended to help users control what kinds of content they are exposed to, so I think photosensitivity would be a valuable addition to that system.\n\nCreators could voluntarily mark avatars or other applicable content as containing intense flashing or potentially photosensitive effects. Users could then choose to hide, restrict, or otherwise be warned about that content through their existing safety settings.\n\nThis would give creators a standardized way to responsibly label visually intense content while giving photosensitive users greater control over what they encounter in VRChat.",
